  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "low",
      "note": "Western hour count (CAR). Frame 'ngbonga {h}' (ngbonga = hour/o'clock), 'ngbonga {h} na ndâmbo' for half, 'ngbonga {h} na minüti <N>' otherwise, with Sango numerals (okü, balë-ôko, balë-ôko na okü, balë-ûse, balë-otâ na okü, balë-usïö, balë-okü ...). Replaced the hour numerals 6-10, which were not standard Sango ('ömënë','mbïrïmbïrï','mënâmbârâ','gonambâlâ','bâlè'), with omanä, mbâsâmbârâ, miombe, gümbâyä, balë-ôko. Doubts: spelling/diacritics of the loan 'minüti' (minute); whether 'na ndâmbo' is the usual way to say half past; noon 'lâ nzönï' and midnight 'gï na lögö' were left untouched but look doubtful ('lâ nzönï' reads like 'good day'). Needs a native speaker."
    }
  ]
